      ":question/problem": "![](images/2b/2bf906050da8bd03f4e72d4c8976fa656131fb46cc3d7fb052d842376be7a353.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is bounded by the planes $y = 0$, $y = 2$, $z = 0$, $z = 1$, $x = 0$, and $x = 4 - y - z$. Given its representation\n$R = {(x, y, z): (y, z) \u2208 D, f_{1}(y, z) \\le x \\le f_{2}(y, z)}$\nas a type II region in three-dimensional space, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $D = {(y, z): 0 \\le y \\le 1, 0 \\le z \\le 2}$\n2. $f_{1}(y, z) = 1$ and $f_{2}(y, z) = 4 - y - z$\n3. $f_{1}(y, z) = 4 - y - z$ and $f_{2}(y, z) = 2$"
