      ":question/problem": "![](images/d2/d294519b3909517b9507322c86ad970550ab388a8d759b0ada99ed18627fc4bd.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is bounded by the planes $y=0$, $y=2$, $z=0$, $z=1$, $x=0,$ and $2x+y=6.$ Given its representation \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,{f}_{1}(y,z)\\le x\\le {f}_{2}(y,z)}\n$$\n\n \nas a type II region in three-dimensional space, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $D={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 1}$\n- ${f}_{1}(y,z)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(y,z)=6-2y$\n- ${f}_{1}(y,z)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(y,z)=\\frac{6-y}{2}$"
